    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41c16891_3ecc355c",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1229,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:20:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we chose staging buffer to map, then the map type would only be `D3D11_MAP_READ_WRITE`, `D3D11_MAP_WRITE`, or `D3D11_MAP_READ`. When staging buffer was chosen, it doesn\u0027t matter map mode is write or read, we want writable because even in read mode we might need to initialize the buffer. So it\u0027s probably easier to use `D3D11_MAP_READ_WRITE` every time.\n\nOn the other hands, if the storage chosen was not staging, then the map type can only be `D3D11_MAP_READ_DISCARD` or `D3D11_MAP_WRITE_OVERWRITE`.\n\nSo TLDR:\n- if mapMode is Write:\n  - Either staging storage or dynamic storage can be chosen\n- if mapMode is Read:\n  - Only staging storage can be chosen.\n- Staging storage and dynamic storage have different `D3D11_MAP` allowed.",
      "parentUuid": "da7ca183_bfe989cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1229,
